VSA MLX runtime
  Selected FastVideo MLX files from 7bb76b5ec99807a66aa3047b901f15019abe0f00
  retain Apache-2.0 and modification notices. See docs/sources.json and
  licenses/FastVideo-APACHE-2.0.txt.
  The sparse attention kernels adapt MLX / mlx-flashattention-steel / MFA
  (MIT) and Draw Things (BSD-3-Clause). Full notices and terms are retained
  in src/h3_apple/runtime/metal/p085_*.txt.
  h3.c decoder kernels: Copyright (c) 2026 Salvatore Sanfilippo, MIT.
  Source 8974cc055ea9c02fcd14cc27dfda3e1027c05153; see metal/p087_NOTICE.txt.
  The W8A8 kernel adapts the pinned vpipe unsigned MMA and affine compensation;
  source and changes are in metal/p138_NOTICE.txt and metal/p139_NOTICE.txt.
  INT8 QK smoothing follows the SageAttention2 paper; no SageAttention code
  is copied into this MLX implementation.
  Kablex/ComfyUI-Ref2VA-VSA (Apache-2.0) informs the gate-only transplant and
  dense-exempt reference prefix. Comfy Kitchen informs the routing semantics;
  complete source identities are retained in docs/sources.json.
  FastH3 gate weights are separately downloaded under the MiniMax H3 terms,
  pinned in data/vsa-gates.json. Only the 50 gate matrices are used; its trained
  T2VA LoRA deltas are not applied. The original LightX2V adapter is fused into
  the VSA checkpoint. No trained weights are bundled.
  data/vae-calibration.npz contains frozen channel maxima, not model weights.
  Its origin/hash are recorded in docs/sources.json; MiniMax-derived material
  remains subject to the model terms.

